  "content": {
    "id": "p44-q9",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "A paddock contains both ducks and sheep.\nThere are a total of 42 heads and 96 feet in the paddock.\nHow many ducks and how many sheep are in the paddock?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "36 ducks and 6 sheep.",
      "worked": "Let $d$ be the number of ducks and $s$ be the number of sheep.\n$$\\begin{align*}d+s&=42\\quad\\text{(1)}\\\\2d+4s&=96\\quad\\text{(2)}\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract $2\\times(1)$ from (2).\n$$\\begin{align*}(2d+4s)-2(d+s)&=96-84\\\\2s&=12\\\\s&=6\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into (1).\n$$\\begin{align*}d+6&=42\\\\d&=36\\end{align*}$$\nThere are 36 ducks and 6 sheep.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
